# Copy to .env for local dev
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
APP_ENV=development

# --- Local-hosting URL knobs (no rebuild required at runtime) ---
# The backend URL resolves in this order (see src/api/baseUrl.js):
#   1. ?api=<url> query param (remembered in that browser; ?api=clear undoes)
#   2. localStorage "onemarket:api-base-url" (Provider Settings page UI)
#   3. window.__ONEMARKET_CONFIG__.API_BASE_URL (public/config.js in dev,
#      dist/config.js after build — edit the file, refresh, done)
#   4. VITE_API_BASE_URL above (baked in at build time)
#   5. smart default (same-origin on https/remote hosts, localhost:8000 locally)
# So for throwaway local runs you can leave this file alone and just use
# ?api= or the settings card. Use config.js / compose env for permanent setups.
#
# `vite dev` proxy for /api (dev-server only, never shipped to the browser):
#   VITE_PROXY_TARGET=http://192.168.1.20:8000 npm run dev
# (BACKEND_URL works as an alias.)
# VITE_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8000
# 1) Local dev (default):          VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
# 2) Vercel monorepo serverless (frontend + api/ in one project):
#    leave VITE_API_BASE_URL UNSET or empty -> client uses same-origin
#    (relative URLs hit /api/* on the same Vercel deployment, no CORS).
# 3) Separate backend (frontend-only deploy):
#    VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://<your-backend-host>   (no trailing slash)
#    + on the backend host set CORS_ORIGINS (or FRONTEND_URL) to this
#    frontend's origin — see infra/oracle/README.md + backend.env.example.
#
# Vercel dashboard: Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables ->
# add VITE_API_BASE_URL (Production and Preview as needed), then Redeploy.
# Changing the baked-in value needs a rebuild, but ?api= / the settings card
# / config.js can still override it at runtime without one.

# --- Backend keys (NOT embedded by Vite; live in infra/docker/.env.example) ---
# Vite only embeds VITE_* at build time. The backend reads these at runtime;
# they are listed here so `grep -r` for required keys finds them, but set the
# real values in infra/docker/.env (local/compose) or the hosting dashboard
# (Vercel/Render), never in a frontend .env that ships to the browser.
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://onemarket:change-me@postgres:5432/onemarket
#   REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0
#   SECRET_KEY=change-me-generate-with-openssl-rand-hex-32
#   CRON_SECRET=
#   APP_ENV=development (above; production on hosted backends)
